      "text": "Given that the roots of the cubic polynomial \\( ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0 \\) are \\( 3 \\) and \\( -2 \\), we can express the polynomial in the factored form as:\n\\[\na(x - 3)(x + 2)(x - r) = 0\n\\]\nwhere \\( r \\) is the third root of the polynomial.\n\nFirst, we expand the factored form:\n\\[\ny = a(x - 3)(x + 2)\n\\]\nExpanding the product \\( (x - 3)(x + 2) \\), we get:\n\\[\n(x - 3)(x + 2) = x^2 - x - 6\n\\]\nThus, the polynomial becomes:\n\\[\ny = a(x^2 - x - 6)\n\\]\nMultiplying by \\( a \\) gives:\n\\[\ny = a(x^2 - x - 6) = ax^2 - ax - 6a\n\\]\n\nWe now have the polynomial:\n\\[\ny = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\n\\]\nBy comparing coefficients with \\( ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d \\), we see:\n\\[\nb = a, \\quad c = -a, \\quad d = -6a\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\( \\frac{b + c}{a} \\):\n\\[\nb + c = a + (-a) = 0\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\n\\frac{b + c}{a} = \\frac{0}{a} = 0\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0}\n\\]",
